<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title><![CDATA[Linklog]]></title><description><![CDATA[Linklog]]></description><link>https://github.com/mondain-dev/linklog</link><generator>RSS for Node</generator><lastBuildDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 23:11:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://mondain-dev.github.io/linklog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title><![CDATA[It seems Piketty has become a degrowther]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6gSPpWEAAAdrP.png:large"></p><p>Thomas Piketty (@PikettyWIL) on X</p><p>The key finding of the report is that energy transition alone will not suffice. We need to combine it with “sufficiency” to stay within 2 degrees. This includes labour hour reductions, growth caps in rich countries, less material consumption, and changes in food habits.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/monday-assorted-links-563.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-563">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:43:05 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1088718721785434112/TCQN0rTD_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X</p><p>This plan is incompatible with freedom- a global class of planners telling us how long to work, how much we can grow, what we can eat. It is also completely wrong. Al